{
  "id": "2026-11-24-discoveryengine-v1alpha",
  "date": "2026-11-24",
  "api": "discoveryengine.v1alpha",
  "service": "Vertex AI Agent Builder",
  "title": "Major API Refactor & UserAvailability Rollback",
  "summary": "The Discovery Engine API has undergone a significant refactor, introducing breaking changes to the `mcp` method and rolling back the recently introduced `UserAvailability` management APIs. Developers must update their integrations to avoid breakage.",
  "details": "This update introduces substantial breaking changes and a rollback of recently added features. The `projects.locations.collections.dataConnector.mcp` method has been refactored: its URI path template changed from `v1alpha/projects/{projectsId}/locations/{locationsId}/collections/{collectionsId}/dataConnector/mcp` to `v1alpha/{+name}/mcp`. The `name` parameter is now strictly required, following the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataConnector`, replacing the individual `projectsId`, `locationsId`, and `collectionsId` parameters. Additionally, the `contentType`, `data`, and `extensions` parameters have been removed from the method signature and are now nested under a new `httpBody` parameter.\n\nCrucially, the `UserAvailability` management APIs, including the `batchUpdate`, `list`, and `update` methods under `projects.locations.userStores.userAvailabilities`, have been entirely removed. All associated schemas, such as `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchUpdateUserAvailabilitiesRequest` and `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaUserAvailability`, are also no longer available. This constitutes a rollback of the feature announced on 2026-11-08.\n\nOn the additive side, two new methods are introduced: `projects.locations.collections.engines.assistants.agents.transferAgentOwner` to transfer ownership of an Agent (requires a `name` parameter), and `projects.locations.collections.engines.sessions.validateUserAuthorization` for validating A2A 3-legged-OAuth consent flows (requires a `session` parameter). Minor schema updates include new `artifactGcsBucket` and `userPrincipalLoggingEnabled` properties in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaObservabilityConfig`, and `preProvisionMode` in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaProvisionProjectRequest`.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "breaking_reasons": [
    "Parameter 'name' was changed to strictly required",
    "Removed parameter 'collectionsId' from method",
    "Removed parameter 'contentType' from method",
    "Removed parameter 'data' from method",
    "Removed parameter 'extensions' from method",
    "Removed parameter 'locationsId' from method",
    "Removed parameter 'projectsId' from method",
    "Removed API method 'batchUpdate'",
    "Removed parameter 'parent' from method",
    "Removed API method 'list'",
    "Removed parameter 'filter' from method",
    "Removed parameter 'pageSize' from method",
    "Removed parameter 'pageToken' from method",
    "Removed API method 'update'",
    "Removed schema 'GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchUpdateUserAvailabilitiesRequest'",
    "Removed schema 'GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaBatchUpdateUserAvailabilitiesResponse'",
    "Removed schema 'GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaListUserAvailabilitiesResponse'",
    "Removed schema 'GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaUpdateUserAvailabilityRequest'",
    "Removed schema 'GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaUserAvailability'",
    "Method 'mcp' URI path template changed from 'v1alpha/projects/{projectsId}/locations/{locationsId}/collections/{collectionsId}/dataConnector/mcp' to 'v1alpha/{+name}/mcp'"
  ],
  "interesting_score": 10,
  "tags": [
    "breaking-change",
    "rollback",
    "new-feature",
    "refactor"
  ],
